// A shop: buying, selling and trading. It shows as an action tile named after
// the shop at its place, and opens a menu of Buy, Sell and Trade lines; lines
// the player can't afford are shown but can't be picked.

== shop wren_shelf
name: Wren's barter shelf
// Where it is, who must be there, and when it is open.
at: clearing
run by: wren
open when: time is day
// What the player pays with: a player value (the coins of rules/interface.fsc),
// or an item (`currency: item copper_coin`); without it, the status bar's currency.
currency: coins
intro:
    Wren clears a space on the flat stone she uses as a counter. 'Coin or trade, I'm not fussy.'
// Shown instead while the shop is closed (at night, or when Wren is away).
closed:
    The flat stone by the lean-to is bare. Wren keeps her wares indoors at night.
// What she sells, and the price. A line can have a condition.
stock:
    herbal_tea: 2
    bandage: 3
    slingshot: 4 [if wren.trust is at least friendly]
// What she buys from the player, and what she pays.
buys:
    wild_berries: 1
    truffle: 3
// Items with `trades for` (items/items.fsc) can be swapped here, and the
// Forager feat sometimes gets a second item thrown in.
trades: yes
trade bonus when: player has feat forager
trade bonus chance: 1 in 3
// After each purchase and sale: [shop.price] is the price ([shop.item] names
// the item too).
bought:
    Wren wraps it in a scrap of cloth. '[shop.price] well spent. Pleasure doing business.'
sold:
    Wren counts out [shop.price] and tucks your goods into her basket.
